#. Tag: title
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:2
#, no-c-format
msgid "Quickguide: Burning an Audio-CD in 4 Steps"
msgstr "Quickguide: Burning an Audio-CD in 4 Steps"

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:5
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This Quickguide shows you how to create a AudioCD with &k3b;. To reproduce "
"these steps you need a working &k3b; and a directory in which you have "
"audiofiles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 1"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you start &k3b; you should see something like this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:15
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can select one of four projects &k3b; offers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:21 audiocd-howto.docbook:38 audiocd-howto.docbook:66
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screenshot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:28
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 2"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:29
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now you click on \"New Audio CD Project\""
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:32
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a dialog where you can select which files you want to burn on a CD"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The files you see on the top-part of &k3b; can be dropped with the mouse to the "
"bottom-widget. Another way is to right-click on a file an select <action>"
"Add to Project</action>. In order to rearrange the order of the audio-tracks "
"you can simply move the tracks with the left mouse-button. The properties of "
"the tracks can be changed by clicking with the &RMB; and choosing <action>"
"Properties</action>. As soon as you like the arrangement of the tracks click on "
"<action>Burn...</action> in the right-bottom corner."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:52
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you burn AudioCD from <acronym>MP3</acronym>s or other lossy compressed "
"music, remember that if you encode this CD back to <acronym>MP3</acronym>"
", you'll get poorer quality regardless the bitrate you use. To check whether "
"AudioCD was burnt from lossy format, try <ulink "
"url=\"http://true-audio.com/analyzer.project\">auCDtect</ulink>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 3"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is a dialog where you can decide the settings for the CD."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this dialog you can control the settings of the burning itself. The "
"default-settings of &k3b; are probably correct for you. In the top-right corner "
"you can control the speed. One last step before the actual burning you can give "
"the CD a title by choosing <guibutton>CD-Text</guibutton> "
"and selecting <guilabel>Write CD-Text</guilabel>. The two which are probably "
"most important for you are <guilabel>Title</guilabel> and <guilabel>"
"Performer</guilabel>. As soon as you are content with the settings click on "
"<guibutton>Burn</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:80
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 4"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "In this dialog you can see the progress of you burning"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: audiocd-howto.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In this dialog is nothing you can do. Just wait for you computer to finish the "
"session."
msgstr ""
